{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.operator_selection_lp","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Int","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fin.VecNotation","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum"],"declarations":8,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_G","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_G","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L194-L195","doc":"`ctxW` carries exactly the witness Gram matrix. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_s","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_s","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L191-L192","doc":"`ctxW` carries exactly the witness multipliers. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_t","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.ctxW_t","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L188-L189","doc":"`ctxW` carries exactly the witness cost vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.exists_lpData_activeSet_gateSet_disjoint","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.exists_lpData_activeSet_gateSet_disjoint","kind":"theorem","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L157-L186","doc":"**The refutation.**\n\nThe witness data satisfy every hypothesis of the operator-selection LP —\nnon-negative multipliers, dual feasibility `tⱼ = y₀ + Σᵢ sᵢGᵢⱼ`, the net\nconstraint, Frobenius positivity, and complementary slackness — and yet\n\n* the active set `{i | 0 < sᵢ}` is non-empty (it is `{1}`);\n* the gate set `{i | tᵢ ≤ 0}` is non-empty (it is `{0}`);\n* the two are **disjoint**.\n\nSo on the program the producer's comment cites, `y_λ* > 0` does not imply\n`t_λ ≤ 0`.  The Pass-2 sign gate is not a consequence of complementary\nslackness — the implication has a counterexample inside the LP itself.\n\nThe same data are packaged as `ctxW`, whose mere type-correctness certifies\nthat they form a genuine `OperatorSelectionLpContext` with a *derived* zero\nduality gap; `ctxW_t`, `ctxW_s` and `ctxW_G` identify its fields with the data\nused here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.complementarySlackness_diagonal_iff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.complementarySlackness_diagonal_iff","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L120-L137","doc":"**Complementary slackness does not mention the cost vector.**\n\nUnder a diagonal Gram the condition `∀ i, sᵢ (Gx)ᵢ = 0` is equivalent to\n`∀ i, sᵢ · G_{ii} · xᵢ = 0`, an equation in the multipliers, the block norms and\nthe *selected operator's* coefficients.  The Markov traces of the atom — the\nproducer's `t_λ` — do not occur.  No predicate on `t` follows from it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.frobeniusValue_of_diagonal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.frobeniusValue_of_diagonal","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L105-L118","doc":"**Orthogonal Wedderburn projectors make the Gram diagonal**, and a diagonal\nGram collapses the Frobenius constraint value to a single product.\n\n`G_{λμ} = tr_M(P_λ P_μ) = δ_{λμ} tr_M(P_λ)` because block projectors are\northogonal idempotents. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.gateSet_eq_tightSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.gateSet_eq_tightSet","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L96-L103","doc":"The same statement for the corpus context, at its own candidate `x*`:\nevery block's Frobenius value is `≥ 0`, so gating on `≤ 0` keeps exactly the\ntight blocks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.frobeniusValue_nonpos_iff_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassTheory.UICGateLP.frobeniusValue_nonpos_iff_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MassTheory/UICGateNotFromComplementarySlackness.lean#L83-L94","doc":"**A Frobenius constraint value cannot be negative on a feasible point.**\n\n`IsFeasible` demands `0 ≤ (Gx)ᵢ` for every `i`, so the predicate `(Gx)ᵢ ≤ 0`\ncollapses to `(Gx)ᵢ = 0`.  \"Sign gate\" and \"tightness gate\" are the same\npredicate when read on a constraint value; they differ only when read on\nsomething that is *not* a constraint value of a feasible point. ","signatureChunk":0}]}